<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells 2,557 tonnes of zinc.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells 2,557 tonnes of zinc.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 5,637,980 lbs, or 2,557 tonnes of zinc, for $3,252,412.</p>
<p>The winning bidders were Allied Deals, Hochschild Partners, Parks Pioneer, Trademet, and American Alloys.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
